Use `T=S+F+U+N` and applicable denominator `A=S+F+U`. Completion rate is `(S+F)/A`, satisfaction rate is `S/A`, and dimension raw score is `W×S/A`. Leave the dimension and overall score unscored if the object set or expansion is unknown. Exclude a dimension from effective weight E when every row is reviewed as not applicable and A is zero. Calculate the overall score only when every dimension can be scored or validly excluded and E is positive. Use 100 times the sum of applicable raw scores divided by E. Round only the displayed result to one decimal place.

Use the historical proposed document threshold of 95 only when the current project adopts it. Retain applicable objects with unavailable environments, pending confirmation, missing research, and unresolved issues. Report critical blockers and actual user confirmation independently of scores.

